[size=3][u][b]🛠 Changelog[/b][/u][/size]

[size=3][u][i][0.10.1] - 2026-10-03[/i][/u][/size]
[list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] A bare name after a table, `$table.frobnicate`, was taken as the value of a key and never reported. A table's keys are read with [b]$[/b] or braces, [b]$table.$name[/b] or `$table.{'name'}`: a bare name is now reported as a property the table does not have. Two of vanilla's own, [b]$TextTable.objective[/b] in [b]gm_escort.xml[/b] and [b]gm_patrol.xml[/b] for `$TextTable.$objective`, show up with it.
[*] A chain that stops inside a property name, [b]$table.keys[/b] for [b]keys.list[/b] or `keys.count`, passed without a finding and gives nothing in the game. It is reported, with the names it may be, and quick fixes complete it to each.
[*] A property a variable's type does not have was not reported under [b]@[/b] or tested with `?`, where the game gives null or false instead of an error; the script still reads what the type does not have, so it is reported there too. In vanilla this shows [b]not @$localtarget.pilot.command[/b] in [b]order.move.recon.xml[/b] (for `command.value`), [b]@$refobject.issuperhighway[/b] on a controllable, [b]@$leaderpilot.escortgroup[/b] on an entity, and two debug texts on a guessed order.
[/list]
[*] Changed
[list]
[*] The MCP server's tools say when to use them, instead of searching the game's schemas, [b]scriptproperties.xml[/b] and text files, and to check every script changed: agents pick tools by their descriptions.
[*] Each call of the MCP server is logged in its output ([b]MCP: List Servers[/b], [b]Show Output[/b]): the tool, its arguments, the time and the size of the answer.
[*] The MCP server is in the MCP Registry, as `io.github.chemodun/x4-script-mcp`, for other editors and agents; with this extension there is no need to add it from VS Code's MCP server gallery.
[*] The README tells where the MCP server is in VS Code, how to start it, and how to get an agent to use it.
[/list]
[/list]
[size=3][u][i][0.10.0] - 2026-10-03[/i][/u][/size]
[list]
[*] Added
[list]
[*] An MCP server for AI agents, offered to the editor's (Copilot's agent mode) on the game files and extensions set here, and on npm as [url=https://www.npmjs.com/package/x4-script-mcp]x4-script-mcp[/url] for other agents: tools that check scripts and patches with their quick fixes, describe an element of the schemas with its attributes and values, resolve an expression such as [b]player.ship.sector[/b] step by step with the properties of the result, find scripts, cues and libraries, go to definition and find references, and look up and search texts. It reads the extensions' files again as the agent changes them. [b]x4CodeSense.mcpServer.enabled[/b] turns it off.
[/list]
[/list]
[size=3][u][i][0.9.0] - 2026-10-03[/i][/u][/size]
[list]
[*] Added
[list]
[*] Patches of the game's library files, in an extension's [b]libraries[/b] folder (`libraries/wares.xml` and the like): applied to the game's file after the patches and merge files of the DLCs and extensions loaded before them, with the problems of their paths, completion, hover and go to definition in them, the status bar, and the diff of the file without and with the patch.
[*] Merge files in `libraries`, whose root is the game file's, merged as the game merges them before the patches loaded after them. A file there whose root is neither [b]diff[/b] nor the game file's is reported (`library-root-mismatch`): the game skips it.
[*] The files of [b]libraries[/b] are in the workspace's problems and in the checks of x4-script-check.
[*] Rename and find all references of a variable, a label or another name also cover the paths of patches that pick an element by a value holding it, such as [b]set_value[@name='$count'][/b] or `do_if[@value='$count gt 0']`: a rename no longer leaves such a path selecting nothing, and is refused when the path is outside the workspace.
[*] Text inside an element that the schema allows to hold only elements, or nothing, is reported as a warning (`text-not-allowed`): a stray [b]>[/b] after a start tag, an attribute typed after its tag was closed. In a patch, also text in [b]<diff>[/b] and `remove`, and text an [b]add[/b] or [b]replace[/b] puts into a script's element.
[*] Well-formedness problems for which the game's parser refuses a file: attributes without whitespace between them, an [b]&[/b] that starts no reference or names an entity XML does not define, a character reference to no character (`&#0;`), [b]--[/b] inside a comment, a [b]<[/b] that starts no tag, text outside the root element, an XML declaration that is not at the very start. The game's files and the mods have none.
[*] Variables have a type when everything that sets them agrees on one: completion after [b]$ship.[/b] offers that type's properties, hover and go to definition of [b]$ship.name[/b] name its property, and hover over [b]$ship[/b] tells the type and what tells it. What actions write is guessed from their names and documentation where the schema does not state it (`create_ship` a ship), and marked "(guessed)"; [b]x4CodeSense.guessVariableTypes[/b] turns the guessing off, [b]--no-type-guesses[/b] in x4-script-check.
[*] A property a variable's type does not have is reported, as for `player.ship`: a warning where the script states the type, information (`expression-unknown-property-guessed`) where it is guessed, worded as the guess it rests on. On the game's own scripts, six, in four files; none in the DLCs.
[*] The extension brings x4-script-check along, [b]dist\x4-script-check.js[/b] in its folder: the scripts can be checked from a command line with Node.js alone, without npm.
[/list]
[*] Changed
[list]
[*] x4-script-check: [b]--game[/b] or [b]--unpacked[/b] given wins over the [b]X4_UNPACKED[/b] and [b]X4_GAME[/b] environment variables; [b]X4_UNPACKED[/b] was taken even with [b]--game[/b] given.
[*] A variable's type comes from the [b]exact[/b] or [b]default[/b] of [b]set_value[/b] and [b]param[/b] only, no longer from that of `create_list`, `append_to_list`, [b]do_all[/b] and the like, where it is a count or the element added; `null`, and a bare `true`, [b]false[/b] or number set before the real value, tell none.
[*] Patches are applied faster where a step of a path picks a node by an attribute's value, such as `cue[@name='Start']`: the node is found without looking at each of its siblings.
[*] A script is checked again faster after each change: the expressions the change left as they were are not parsed again, nor their properties looked up again. In the largest scripts, about a quarter less time per change.
[*] Hover over a step of a patch's path names an element without [b]name[/b] by its `id`.
[*] A patch operation that does what X4CodeSense does not model, a change of text or an added namespace, is reported as such (`patch-operation-unsupported`, information) instead of being taken as applied. An operation that adds an element next to the root element, removes the root or adds into a comment says what the result would be, no longer that the game skips it.
[/list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] In the diff of a patch, the file's document type declaration is kept, and the end tag of an element that gets its first child ends its line with the file's line break.
[*] Text typed inside an element in the side with the patch was dropped without a word when the side was written; the change is now refused, with the reason.
[*] A variable read after an [b]include_actions[/b] whose [b]ref[/b] is a value, such as `$Thread.$NameLib`, was reported as never set, though the library chosen at run time may set it. Eight such findings in the game's own scripts are gone.
[*] XPath in a patch that the game evaluates but X4CodeSense does not, such as `(//move_to)[1]`, [b]//a and //b[/b] in [b]if[/b] or `@name = 'x'`, was reported as an error; it is information now, as other XPath not understood.
[*] `silent="1"`, as the DLCs' patches write it, was not taken as silent.
[*] A path comparing an attribute's value now takes a line break or tab in it as a space, as the game's parser does; and a comment in the text of an operation that sets a value is no longer part of the value.
[*] A script whose root start tag lost its [b]>[/b] lost every check and feature; it keeps them now, with the unclosed tag reported.
[*] In a file that starts with a byte order mark, columns on its first line were one too far in x4-script-check, in the problems of files checked from disk, and where go to definition or rename from another file leads.
[*] [b]</[/b] typed for an end tag gave two errors about an empty name, and a value whose quote was just opened was reported as invalid.
[*] A value of type `xs:positiveInteger`, such as [b]sinceversion[/b] of `patch`, could be 0.
[*] A bare name after a list, a number, a string or an object was taken as a value of its placeholder, [b]cargo.frob[/b] as `cargo.{$numeric}`, and never reported; only ids such as the terraforming projects' (`project.agr_fields_sunrise`) are written so. A braced step after a list, `subordinates.{$i}`, may be its index or a longer property, so no type follows it.
[*] Typing [b]player.ship.[/b] gave a second warning, about a property '' of the ship, beside the syntax error.
[*] Numbers with the units `km`, `ms`, `min`, `h`, `deg`, [b]Cr[/b] and `LF`, and values cast to a unit (`(1 + 1)s`), had no type; a number with a fraction was taken as an integer.
[*] In a patch, the message of a property a variable's type lacks named a line of the patched file, not of the patch.
[*] [b]%%d[/b] (a percent sign and a d) was reported as `%d`, and a format with [b]%d[/b] got a second finding about its arguments. A string holding a text reference, `'{1001, 2}'.[$a]`, is no longer counted as a format without placeholders.
[*] The signature help of a format went away right after the [b]][/b] of a format in its arguments, and miscounted after an escaped quote (`'it\'s'`).
[*] What a library of another script sets was not followed while it was edited: a script that includes it kept its findings until it was edited itself. Now the scripts that include, instantiate or run a library are checked again once typing pauses in it.
[*] Typing a cue's name, or in a text file, analysed every other open document at once, on each keystroke; they are analysed once typing pauses.
[*] The variables of a library or cue a patch adds were not seen by the scripts that include it or name them as `md.Script.Cue.$x`.
[*] A read under `do_if value="not $x?"`, or beside `$x? or …`, was taken as safe, though the body runs without `$x`.
[*] An extension created or copied into the workspace while VS Code ran was not read until a restart.
[*] A text file edited under a path whose case differs from the one read at the start, as VS Code writes the drive letter, was read twice.
[*] Completion of child elements offered every child of the parent where the schema allows no more; it offers none there now.
[*] Renaming a cue left its bare names in a library of another script that the cue's script includes, and renaming a label left those in an interrupt library item the script uses, without a word: the game then no longer finds them. Find all references lists them now, and the rename takes them or is refused, with the reason.
[*] Renaming an AI script name or an order id showed VS Code's "The element can't be renamed."; it gives the reason now.
[*] Find all references of a name used in many files is two to three times faster: the texts of those files are kept between requests.
[*] A setting of another type than declared, such as [b]null[/b] for a folder in settings.json, stopped the language server from reading the settings: no game files, no status, well-formedness only. It counts as the default now. The same happened in an LSP client that refuses to register for configuration changes.
[*] [b]x4CodeSense.languageNumber[/b] with leading zeros, [b]007[/b] as in the name `0001-l007.xml`, showed English texts.
[*] A folder deleted on disk, a mod or one a checkout removed, left its scripts in the index and their problems in the Problems panel: VS Code reports the folder alone, not the files in it.
[*] x4-script-check checked a folder given twice, or inside another given folder, twice: every finding was reported twice.
[*] [b]--fix[/b] of x4-script-check wrote a file that is not UTF-8 back with a replacement character for each of its other characters; it leaves such a file as it is now, and says so.
[/list]
[/list]
[size=3][u][i][0.8.0] - 2026-10-01[/i][/u][/size]
[list]
[*] Added
[list]
[*] The installed game as the game files, nothing to extract: `x4CodeSense.gameFolder`, set with [b]Select the Installed Game...[/b], also from the status bar's menu. Its files and its DLCs' are read straight from their catalogs, and open read-only where go to definition, references and [b]Open the File This Patch Changes[/b] lead.
[*] The status bar's tooltip tells where the game files come from, and the installed game's version.
[*] The command-line checker reads an installed game with `--game`: its files and its DLCs' straight from their catalogs, without extracting them.
[/list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] An extension linked into a folder of extensions, as modders and mod managers do with a junction or a symbolic link, is found.
[/list]
[/list]
[size=3][u][i][0.7.0] - 2026-10-01[/i][/u][/size]
[list]
[*] Added
[list]
[*] The command-line checker applies the preferred fixes with `--fix`, and writes SARIF for GitHub code scanning with `--format sarif`.
[*] Quick fixes that create what nothing defines: a cue or library, also in the script [b]md.Script.Cue[/b] names, a label, and a parameter a call passes in the script, order or library it calls.
[*] Quick fixes for tags and children: a value or start tag left open is closed, a missing end tag added, an end tag that matches nothing renamed or removed, a required child added, a child moved where the schema allows it; and for the step of a patch's [b]sel[/b] that selects nothing, the names the file has there.
[*] Completion of text references in any XML file, such as wares, macros and the text files, not only in scripts.
[*] Signature help for the arguments of a format, [b]'%s of %s'.[…][/b] or `{page, id}.[…]`, with the placeholder of the argument at the caret highlighted.
[*] A warning for a format given fewer arguments than it takes, and information for arguments it does not show.
[*] The README tells where X4CodeSense takes its knowledge from, and what is built in.
[/list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] A value whose text ends in `name=`, such as [b]comment="… instead of otherobject="[/b] in [b]gs_pirate1.xml[/b] of the Tides of Avarice DLC, is no longer taken for an unclosed value followed by another attribute.
[/list]
[/list]
[size=3][u][i][0.6.0] - 2026-10-01[/i][/u][/size]
[list]
[*] Added
[list]
[*] The problems of every script and patch in the workspace, not only of the open ones, when [b]x4CodeSense.diagnosticMode[/b] is `workspace`; [b]Choose Which Scripts Show Problems[/b] sets it, also from the status bar's menu.
[*] Apply all preferred fixes in this file: in the light bulb, and as [b]source.fixAll[/b] for `editor.codeActionsOnSave`.
[*] A warning for an AI script name or order id that a call writes as is and no script defines, with a quick fix to the known name it is close to.
[*] The outline shows an order's name as the game shows it.
[/list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] After a start of VS Code, the scripts in the restored tabs show their problems, not only the one in front.
[*] X4CodeSense starts with a workspace that holds scripts, before a script is opened.
[/list]
[/list]
[size=3][u][i][0.5.0] - 2026-10-01[/i][/u][/size]
[list]
[*] Added
[list]
[*] Go to Symbol in Workspace: the scripts, cues, libraries and interrupt library items of the game, its DLCs, the extensions and the workspace, also as `md.Script.Cue`.
[*] The parameters of calls (`run_script`, `create_order`, `run_actions`, `<cue ref>`, …): signature help, completion of the parameter names, hover with their description and default, and go to their declaration.
[*] A warning for a parameter a call passes that its target does not declare, with a quick fix to the declared name it is close to. The game's own scripts have four, left behind when a library changed.
[*] AI script names and order ids in calls (`run_script name="'move.generic'"`, `create_order id="'Attack'"`): completion, hover with an order's name and description, go to definition, and find all references, also from [b]<aiscript name>[/b] and `<order id>`.
[/list]
[/list]
[size=3][u][i][0.4.1] - 2026-10-01[/i][/u][/size]
[list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] A patch opened in the group of the diff, such as from the Explorer while the diff has the focus, moves to the patches as before, and now its diff opens below it.
[/list]
[*] Changed
[list]
[*] Typing in large scripts is faster: semantic highlighting takes up to half the time it took, the checks up to a tenth less.
[/list]
[/list]
[size=3][u][i][0.4.0] - 2026-10-01[/i][/u][/size]
[list]
[*] Added
[list]
[*] Both sides of the diff of a patch have the script's hover, go to definition, references, outline and semantic highlighting, and the side with the patch its completion and quick fixes. That side shows the problems the file before the patch does not have, also what the patch breaks elsewhere in the script.
[/list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] A folder added to the workspace while the game files are still read is no longer left out of the index until a restart.
[/list]
[/list]
[size=3][u][i][0.3.0] - 2026-10-01[/i][/u][/size]
[list]
[*] Added
[list]
[*] [b]Edit This Patch Above What It Changes[/b]: the patch above the diff of the file it changes, and the caret follows between them. The side with the patch can be edited: typing in what the patch brings in goes into the patch at once; saving the side writes its other changes into the patch as new operations, with full paths, in the order of the places they change.
[*] While the window is arranged so, a file opened in the diff's group moves up to the patch's, and the diff follows the patch in front above.
[/list]
[*] Changed
[list]
[*] In the diff of a patch, what an operation brings in is shown at the column of the element it replaces or is added next to, or one step deeper than the element it is added into, instead of its column in the patch.
[*] A patch's diffs close with the patch.
[/list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] A diff of a patch restored from the last session gets its text once the game files are read.
[/list]
[/list]
[size=3][u][i][0.2.2] - 2026-09-30[/i][/u][/size]
[list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] Hover over a property whose name goes on after it, such as [b]mayattack[/b] in `$ship.mayattack.{$faction}`, shows that property and every variant that fits as well. When the type of [b]$ship[/b] was not known, it showed unrelated [b]{$numeric}[/b] properties.
[*] Completion after such a name offers its [b]{…}[/b] variants first, also when the type before it is not known: [b]$ship.mayattack.[/b] offers [b]{$component}[/b] and `{$faction}`.
[*] A bare value such as [b]argon[/b] is taken only where [b]scriptproperties.xml[/b] declares a shortcut for it (`isclass.<classname>`, `skill.<skillname>`), and completion offers bare values only there.
[/list]
[/list]
